"""A departure board baked into the firmware, shown when the API is down.

A real weekday morning at Stoke Mandeville: seven trains to London
Marylebone, and the stations the first of them calls at. Shown only once a
fetch has failed and nothing has ever been fetched successfully. Once a fetch
succeeds the live board replaces this and never goes back to it.

Both are stored exactly as the API returned them, and parsed by the same code
as live responses, so changing how responses are read does not mean
regenerating them.

Regenerate with a busy weekday hour, then the first service it lists:
  GET https://data.rtt.io/gb-nr/location
      ?code=SKM&filterTo=MYB&timeFrom=<date>T07:00:00&timeTo=<date>T09:30:00
  GET https://data.rtt.io/rtt/service?uniqueIdentity=<first uniqueIdentity>
"""

